# gogdl — built FROM SOURCE via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD (packages/gogdl/PKGBUILD), NOT fetched
# from the holo monorepo: like legendary it is AUR-only, absent from holo core and extra aarch64
# (checked against build/snapshot.pin). Same "local PKGBUILD" form as packages/f3/source.pin.
#
# Why: the GOG half of alien-games milestone 1 (.claude/plans/alien-games.plan.md). Nothing in the
# image calls it yet — this milestone lands inert on purpose.
#
# Version: 1.3.0, upstream's latest tag.
#
# UNLIKE legendary, THIS ONE IS NOT ARCH-INDEPENDENT. gogdl builds a C extension (gogdl_xdelta3)
# around a vendored xdelta3, so the package is aarch64 and the PKGBUILD carries TWO sources — the
# xdelta3 tree is a git submodule and GitHub's archive tarball ships that directory EMPTY. The
# PKGBUILD header has the detail; the offline suite (tests/test-store-cli.sh) asserts the second
# source stays pinned to the commit upstream's .gitmodules names.
#
# Fields (see packages/README.md):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel so pacman prefers our build
#
# To bump gogdl: edit pkgver + sha256sums in packages/gogdl/PKGBUILD, AND re-read the submodule
# commit out of the new tag's .gitmodules — a version bump that leaves _xdelta_commit stale builds
# green against the wrong xdelta3. Then `make relock`.
name: gogdl
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
